@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

# Scenariusz audit logu (po `docker compose exec api npx knex seed:run`):
# utworzenie -> kolizja 409 -> anulowanie przez ADMINa -> ponowne anulowanie -> audit log

### Login: Jan (właściciel rezerwacji)
# @name jan
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "jan.kowalski@example.com", "password": "bardzo-dlugie-haslo" }

### Login: Anna (próba kolizji)
# @name anna
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "anna.nowak@example.com", "password": "bardzo-dlugie-haslo" }

### Login: ADMIN
# @name admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@example.com", "password": "admin-haslo-123" }

### 1. Jan tworzy rezerwację -> 201 (event reservation.created)
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{jan.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "participants": 5,
  "startTime": "2027-03-10T10:00:00Z",
  "endTime": "2027-03-10T11:00:00Z"
}

### 2. Anna rezerwuje ten sam termin -> 409 ROOM_ALREADY_BOOKED (brak eventu)
POST {{baseUrl}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{anna.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 1,
  "participants": 3,
  "startTime": "2027-03-10T10:30:00Z",
  "endTime": "2027-03-10T11:30:00Z"
}

### 3. ADMIN anuluje rezerwację Jana -> 200 (event reservation.cancelled + [notification] w logach api)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reservations/{{created.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. Ponowne anulowanie -> 200, idempotentne (brak eventu)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reservations/{{created.response.body.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5. Audit log (ADMIN) - od najnowszych
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/audit-log
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6. Audit log z filtrem eventType
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/audit-log?eventType=reservation.cancelled
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. Audit log jako USER -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/audit-log
Authorization: Bearer {{jan.response.body.accessToken}}
